  "section_notes": "The final text keeps the 5% test cap and per-model results to purchasers and regulators but not the public, yet gives existing models up to a 5-year remediation window, which is well beyond the 36-month limit for acceptable transitions and so makes S2 weakened. S5 sets an 8-per-100,000 mandatory recall with a time-limited regulator-approved alternative, which is acceptable under the rules but exposes models like Ember 8 (9.9) to recall unless the alternative is ordered. S3's 6-year retrofit deadline and S4's 36-month suppression start both fall within acceptable ranges, and S1 is fully safe with 48-hour reporting of all thermal incidents."
